    "perplexity": {
      "description": "To See the Lights is Gene’s 1996 compilation of B-sides, live recordings, radio sessions, and cover versions, issued on Costermonger as a companion piece to the band’s early singles era. Rather than a conventional studio album, it gathers the material that surrounded Gene’s first wave of releases, showing the group’s sharp melodic instincts, literate lyricism, and clear debt to indie pop and Britpop while also highlighting a rougher, more immediate live edge.\n\nThe record reached No. 11 in the UK album chart, which underlined how strongly Gene’s audience responded to the band’s non-album material. Its track selection includes early signature songs, alternate versions, and notable covers, making it valuable both as an archive of the group’s formative period and as a coherent listening experience in its own right; later deluxe reissues expanded the set with additional material.",
